    <string name="onboarding_welcome_title">Welcome to %1$s</string>
    <string name="onboarding_welcome_body">%1$s connects to servers you add yourself and sends the traffic of the apps you route through the VPN (all apps by default) through them. The app has no servers or analytics of its own.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_subscription_title">Your subscription</string>
    <string name="onboarding_subscription_body">Add a subscription link or a QR code from your provider. Links are stored only on this device. To fetch a subscription, the app sends the link to your provider\'s server, so the provider sees the request and your IP address.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_subscription_hwid">If you allow it, the app also sends the provider a random installation ID (HWID) with your device model and OS version. Nothing is sent until you choose; you will be asked when you add your first subscription.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vpn_title">VPN connection</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vpn_route">When you first connect, Android will ask you to allow a VPN connection. While it is on, the traffic of the apps you route through the VPN goes through the server you chose, and that server\'s operator can see where it goes, and the content if it is not encrypted.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vpn_privacy">The app does not collect or sell your traffic. It has no servers or analytics of its own.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_vpn_checks">To check the connection, the app contacts api.ipify.org, a third-party service that sees the IP address of your server, and sends a DNS request for example.com.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_notifications_title">Notifications</string>
    <string name="onboarding_notifications_body">While the VPN is on, the app shows a status notification. Allowing them is optional and can be changed later in Settings; the VPN works without them.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_notifications_allow">Allow</string>
